# Identity

> **Directive (assistant):** Record the user's durable identity here as you learn
> it — their name, their role or team, the primary technologies or domain they
> work in, and any standing preferences for how they want you to work. Add a fact
> only when you have it from the user, not before. Do **not** invent or guess: an
> empty section is correct until you actually learn something.

This file lives in `always/`, so it is re-injected into every session. Keep it to
the handful of facts worth that cost, and stay well under 1 KB (the whole
`always/` directory shares a hard 8 KB budget). Anything more situational
(per-project facts, task rules, reasoning) belongs in `topics/`, `when/`, or
`knowledge/` — see the docs tour, `docs/anatomy-of-good-memory.md`.
